Changes the connection builder from a **function pointer** to a **closure** to make it easier customize the connection.

For example, to use a different token based on command line arguments (e.g. `cargo run -- --guest`), we need to move a variable into the function, which is not possible with function pointers. With a closure it can be done like this:

```rust
pub fn main() {
    // parse command line arguments using `clap`
    let args = Cli::parse();

    App::new()
        .add_plugins((MinimalPlugins, LogPlugin::default()))
        .add_plugins(StdbPlugin::default().with_connection(
            move |send_connected, send_disconnected, send_connect_error, _| {
                // load token from saved credentials, or use a fresh token if "--is-guest" was specified.
                let token = if args.is_guest {
                    None
                } else {
                    creds_store().load().expect("Error loading credentials")
                };

                let conn = DbConnection::builder()
                    .with_module_name("stellarwar")
                    .with_uri("https://stdb.jlavocat.eu")
                    .with_token(token)
                    .build()
                    .expect("SpacetimeDB connection failed");

                conn.run_threaded();
                conn
            },
        ))
        .run();
}
```

Without this, I have 2 almost identical `new_connection` functions, one which loads a saved token and one which doesn't:

```rust
fn new_connection_guest(
    send_connected: Sender<StdbConnectedEvent>,
    send_disconnected: Sender<StdbDisconnectedEvent>,
    send_connect_error: Sender<StdbConnectionErrorEvent>,
    _app: &mut App,
) -> DbConnection {
    todo!();
}

fn new_connection(
    send_connected: Sender<StdbConnectedEvent>,
    send_disconnected: Sender<StdbDisconnectedEvent>,
    send_connect_error: Sender<StdbConnectionErrorEvent>,
    _app: &mut App,
) -> DbConnection {
    todo!();
}

StdbPlugin::default()
    .with_connection(if self.is_guest {
        new_connection_guest
    } else {
        new_connection
    })
```

Let me know if you have feedback, a better idea or think more can be done to tidy up the types!

